What is here. These files are MiSTer-devel/NES_MiSTer (https://github.com/MiSTer-devel/NES_MiSTer), commit 49a0a66
(2026-09-30), copied unchanged by tools/vendor_nes_mister.sh (SHA256SUMS lists them): the machine (nes.v, ppu.sv, apu.sv,
cart.sv), the mapper files (mappers/), the package of savestate register constants (regs_savestates.sv) and the VHDL 6502 (t65/,
T65 by Daniel Wallner and others, with the MiSTer changes). Ludvig Strigeus' copyright and the "This program is GPL Licensed"
headers are in the files; COPYING is the licence text, GNU GPL version 3.

What is built from them is NOT these files. cores/nes/gen is what tools/nes_gen.py makes of them, and only gen/ goes into the
bitstream. Every change the generator makes is mechanical and counted (the generator fails when upstream stops matching):
a clock enable on every clocked process, the MiSTer savestate registers replaced by their default values, the wired-or
(tri0/tri1) nets of cart.sv made an explicit OR/AND over the mappers that are built, the mappers that are not built left out,
and the 6502 converted from VHDL to Verilog by GHDL (so that Verilator and Vivado read the same source).

What the licence means here. GPL v3 covers the gateware of this core and everything linked into its partial bitstream
(nes_partial.bit). A .cor or partial bitstream of this core that is given to a third party has to come with its corresponding
source: that is this directory (the upstream copy), cores/nes/gen (the generated source), cores/nes/trx and
cores/nes/layer2_nes.v (our glue: frame writer, registers, DDR2 window and line caches, audio, the partition's edge),
tools/nes_gen.py and tools/vendor_nes_mister.sh (the generator), and the build recipe cores/nes/mono/build_mono.tcl with
cores/nes/nes_timing.tcl - all of it is in this repository. The
host (layer 1), the other cores and the applications are separate works in separate partial bitstreams, link nothing of this
core and are not covered; host/ is not part of this core's build.

cores/nes/trx/nes_regs.v decodes an iNES header into the machine's mapper_flags word the way GameLoader in NES_MiSTer's NES.sv
(same commit; NES.sv itself is not vendored, it is the board top) does, so that part is derived from GPL v3 code and carries the
same licence.

NES software is copyrighted by others. No cartridge image (ROM) is in this repository, in a bench, in a package or in a .cor,
ever; the benches run a program that is written in the bench itself.

Not copied, on purpose: the MiSTer framework and board parts (sys/, sdram.sv, ddram.sv, pll*,
video.sv, composite_*, miracle.sv, keyboard.sv, zapper.sv, dsp.v, cheatcodes.sv, EEPROM_24C0x.sv), the savestate framework
(savestates.vhd, statemanager.vhd, bus_savestates.vhd, savestate_ui.sv, the eReg_SavestateV register), the .mif/.chr/.bin/.asm
data files, the Quartus project files and NES.sv.
